H('405.d.10.E',4,"Combining a motor from one idea with a sensor from another to make a new concept is called:","synthesis of alternatives",["subtraction","erasure","repetition"],"Concept synthesis builds new solutions.")
H('405.d.10.F',3,"Tools such as simulation or a test rig help a team to:","evaluate a proposed solution",["avoid testing","hide errors","sell products"],"Tools support evaluation.")
H('405.d.10.F',4,"Running a computer simulation before building a multi-system product can reveal:","design problems early",["a marketing plan","a lunch menu","a team name"],"Early detection saves cost.")
H('405.d.10.G',3,"A justified solution is supported by data and the:","requirements it meets",["team's mascot","logo color","weather"],"Justification cites requirements.")
H('405.d.10.G',4,"Selecting the preferred multi-system solution using a weighted matrix shows the use of:","structured decision-making",["luck","favoritism","guessing"],"Structure reduces bias.")
H('405.d.11.A',3,"A presentation for a complex solution should be adapted to the audience's:","level of technical knowledge",["shoe size","favorite food","hair color"],"Know your audience.")
H('405.d.11.A',4,"When presenting to non-engineers, a speaker should:","avoid unexplained jargon",["use more jargon","speak faster","read slides aloud"],"Plain language helps.")
H('405.d.11.B',3,"Asking the audience to rate the clarity of a presentation is a way to:","solicit feedback",["end the talk","hide errors","trade grades"],"Ask for input.")
H('405.d.11.B',4,"Feedback is most useful when it identifies:","specific strengths and areas to improve",["only praise","only criticism","personal traits"],"Specific feedback guides growth.")
H('405.d.11.C',3,"Writing about essential skills gained in a project is part of:","reflection",["manufacturing","shipping","purchasing"],"Reflection captures learning.")
H('405.d.11.C',4,"Setting a goal to learn a new software tool after a project is an example of:","planning for growth",["avoiding learning","ending a career","ignoring lessons"],"Reflection leads to goals.")

H('406.d.1',3,"An engineer learns a client plans to use her sensor design in a weapon that could harm civilians illegally. She should:","refuse and consult her ethics code",["ignore it","delete the design","sell it to others"],"Ethical codes put public welfare first.")
H('406.d.1',4,"When a company asks an engineer to falsify a test report, the engineer should:","decline and report the request",["comply","blame a colleague","quietly delay"],"Integrity is non-negotiable.")
H('406.d.2.A',3,"A student watching a ball roll farther on carpet than on tile asks, 'Why does surface type change the distance?' This is an example of:","a question based on observation",["a conclusion","a law","a data table"],"Questions come from observations.")
H('406.d.2.A',4,"A well-defined engineering problem names a need and a way to:","measure success",["avoid testing","delay work","skip research"],"Measurable problems can be solved.")
